Survival Studio: third-party material

Code
  libzim (GPL-2.0-or-later) reads ZIM files. It comes from the distribution package (libzim-dev) and is linked
  dynamically; its dependency libxapian (GPL-2.0-or-later) comes with it. Neither is copied into this repository.
  zlib (zlib licence) inflates PMTiles directories and tiles.

Formats
  ZIM (openZIM), PMTiles (Protomaps, BSD-3-Clause specification) and Mapbox Vector Tile (the open tile encoding)
  are read by code written for taOS from the public format descriptions.

Data (never in the repository; downloaded or imported by the person into their own data folder)
  catalog/packs.json lists packs with the publisher's own checksums and licences. The Wikipedia packs are CC BY-SA 4.0
  (Wikipedia contributors, packaged by Kiwix). Map packs made from the Protomaps basemap carry OpenStreetMap data
  under the ODbL: the attribution is shown on the map and in the pack list.

Catalogues
  catalog/collections.json is derived from the curated tiers of Project N.O.M.A.D. (collections/kiwix-categories.json,
  https://github.com/Crosstalk-Solutions/project-nomad, Apache-2.0, Copyright Crosstalk Solutions, LLC): the choice of
  packs and their grouping. catalog/models.json lists the models that project offers. catalog/regions.json names its
  ready-made US map files. The packs themselves come from their publishers (Kiwix, Learning Equality, Protomaps, the
  OpenStreetMap contributors) and are never in this repository. The Kiwix OPDS catalogue and the Kolibri catalogue
  are read at run time.

Scenario lists
  catalog/scenarios.json holds quantities and item names as plain facts from Ready.gov (US Department of Homeland Security, FEMA)
  and from the UK Government's Be Ready campaign (Open Government Licence v3.0, Crown copyright); no text is copied,
  each source is linked inside the file with its terms. Lines marked 'taOS assumption' or source 'taos' are ours.

Icons
  The application icon (icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/my.taos.survival.svg) was drawn for taOS from plain shapes.
  The line icons in Taos.Apps Glyph.qml (the set this app uses, with the ones added for it) are Lucide/Feather derived:

